I think it might be good for you to re-read the README, BUILD, and DESIGN documents to recall the spirit. Trying to rediscover the wheel that HTML offers. Pandoc should not be needed to create high-quality, rich, documents including academic writing. We already have a tool that renders structured text--the browser. We just have never built the tooling to make it work for this application. Because html is hard to type and read, we need a shorthand that tries to approach the simplicity of markdown without sacrificing the richness of html, but without recreating that with arbitrary adornments. This is the philosophy.
